OL,0,        ECIMSBWebfax 2   F124A1772999460
OL,1,W{$~sj5j5h7}j7}                 G1/9
OL,2,W/*%+,"-/.!/*%/*-'Q(,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,
OL,3,GFEATURESCSuspension of daytime BBC Two
OL,4,Ctransmitter shutdown due to Channel 4
OL,5,Claunch
OL,6,
OL,7,FA recovered Ceefax page sheds some
OL,8,Flight on how tight BBC budgets
OL,9,Frestricted BBC Two's transmission time
OL,10,Ffor many years.
OL,12,FFrom 1st October 1982, BBC Two's
OL,13,Ffour-hour transmitter shutdown after
OL,14,FPlay School was suspended for four
OL,15,Fmonths.
OL,17,FThe channel's trade test transmissions
OL,18,Fwere sharply curtailed in January 1975
OL,19,Fto help the corporation deal with a
OL,20,Fcash crisis and support a wider drive
OL,21,Facross the country to conserve fuel.
OL,23,APub: 22-Jul-2025Qpppppppppppppppppppppp
OL,24,ANext Page BRewind CNat Radio FNat Sport
FL,125,120,200,300,0,100
PN,12402
SC,0002
CT,3,C
PS,c008
OL,0,        ECIMSBWebfax 2   F124A1772999460
OL,1,W{$~sj5j5h7}j7}                 G2/9
OL,2,W/*%+,"-/.!/*%/*-'Q(,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,
OL,3,GFEATURESCSuspension of daytime BBC Two
OL,4,Ctransmitter shutdown due to Channel 4
OL,5,Claunch
OL,6,
OL,7,FGenerally BBC Two transmitters were
OL,8,Fonly on the air from 10.30am to 11.30am
OL,9,Fand from 4pm onwards. In 1980 there was
OL,10,Fa slight extension when Ceefax
OL,11,FIn-Vision was introduced.
OL,13,FThe Ceefax page from September 1982
OL,14,Fexplains the rationale for the planned
OL,15,Ftemporary lifting of the restriction.
OL,17,FThe extra hours of BBC Two trade test
OL,18,Ftransmissions were to help aerial
OL,19,Friggers support the launch of Channel
OL,20,F4.
OL,23,APub: 22-Jul-2025Qpppppppppppppppppppppp
OL,24,ANext Page BRewind CNat Radio FNat Sport
FL,125,120,200,300,0,100
PN,12403
SC,0003
CT,3,C
PS,c008
OL,0,        ECIMSBWebfax 2   F124A1772999460
OL,1,W{$~sj5j5h7}j7}                 G3/9
OL,2,W/*%+,"-/.!/*%/*-'Q(,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,
OL,3,GFEATURESCSuspension of daytime BBC Two
OL,4,Ctransmitter shutdown due to Channel 4
OL,5,Claunch
OL,6,
OL,7,FI suspect the decision to do this was
OL,8,Ftaken some time in advance.
OL,10,FThe clue is in the wording of the page
OL,11,F` contrary to what it says, C4 and the
OL,12,FIBA were actually running trade tests
OL,13,Ffrom the start of August.
OL,15,FSo why were BBC Two's trade tests
OL,16,Fbriefly extended?
OL,18,FGenerally, aerials did not need to be
OL,19,Fadjusted for C4. Sets simply needed
OL,20,Ftuned in.
OL,23,APub: 22-Jul-2025Qpppppppppppppppppppppp
OL,24,ANext Page BRewind CNat Radio FNat Sport
FL,125,120,200,300,0,100
PN,12404
SC,0004
CT,3,C
PS,c008
OL,0,        ECIMSBWebfax 2   F124A1772999460
OL,1,W{$~sj5j5h7}j7}                 G4/9
OL,2,W/*%+,"-/.!/*%/*-'Q(,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,
OL,3,GFEATURESCSuspension of daytime BBC Two
OL,4,Ctransmitter shutdown due to Channel 4
OL,5,Claunch
OL,6,
OL,7,FThe UHF transmission system was
OL,8,Fdesigned to allow for national coverage
OL,9,Fby four channels.
OL,11,FAn aerial properly set up for the three
OL,12,Fexisting channels could be presumed to
OL,13,Fbe set up for good C4 reception.
OL,15,FBut there were specific exceptions.
OL,17,FOccasionally C4 was on an unusual
OL,18,Ffrequency because of the risk of
OL,19,Finterfering with continental
OL,20,Ftransmissions.
OL,23,APub: 22-Jul-2025Qpppppppppppppppppppppp
OL,24,ANext Page BRewind CNat Radio FNat Sport
FL,125,120,200,300,0,100
PN,12405
SC,0005
CT,3,C
PS,c008
OL,0,        ECIMSBWebfax 2   F124A1772999460
OL,1,W{$~sj5j5h7}j7}                 G5/9
OL,2,W/*%+,"-/.!/*%/*-'Q(,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,
OL,3,GFEATURESCSuspension of daytime BBC Two
OL,4,Ctransmitter shutdown due to Channel 4
OL,5,Claunch
OL,6,
OL,7,FIn these localities, existing aerials
OL,8,Fmay have needed replaced.
OL,10,FThere was another factor to consider.
OL,12,FBy 1982, some relays existed merely to
OL,13,Fprovide improved reception ` unlike the
OL,14,Ffirst relays which extended coverage
OL,15,Finto areas with no usable UHF signal.
OL,23,APub: 22-Jul-2025Qpppppppppppppppppppppp
OL,24,ANext Page BRewind CNat Radio FNat Sport
FL,125,120,200,300,0,100
PN,12406
SC,0006
CT,3,C
PS,c008
OL,0,        ECIMSBWebfax 2   F124A1772999460
OL,1,W{$~sj5j5h7}j7}                 G6/9
OL,2,W/*%+,"-/.!/*%/*-'Q(,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,
OL,3,GFEATURESCSuspension of daytime BBC Two
OL,4,Ctransmitter shutdown due to Channel 4
OL,5,Claunch
OL,6,
OL,7,FIn these cases, some may have
OL,8,Fcontemplated two aerials- one for
OL,9,Fexcellent reception of the three
OL,10,Fexisting channels, another turned to
OL,11,Fthe main transmitter for a usable (if
OL,12,Fghosty or grainy) C4 signal.
OL,14,FI suspect though that very few people
OL,15,Fwould actually have gone to the trouble
OL,16,Fof getting a new aerial just to get C4.
OL,18,FEither way, it Is telling that the BBC
OL,19,Fdidn't make the extension to BBC Two's
OL,20,Ftransmission time permanent straight
OL,21,Faway.
OL,23,APub: 22-Jul-2025Qpppppppppppppppppppppp
OL,24,ANext Page BRewind CNat Radio FNat Sport
FL,125,120,200,300,0,100
PN,12407
SC,0007
CT,3,C
PS,c008
OL,0,        ECIMSBWebfax 2   F124A1772999460
OL,1,W{$~sj5j5h7}j7}                 G7/9
OL,2,W/*%+,"-/.!/*%/*-'Q(,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,
OL,3,GFEATURESCSuspension of daytime BBC Two
OL,4,Ctransmitter shutdown due to Channel 4
OL,5,Claunch
OL,6,
OL,7,FOn 7th February 1983, the 11.30am
OL,8,Fshutdown returned. It was finally
OL,9,Fabandoned by stealth when schools
OL,10,Fprogrammes moved to BBC Two seven
OL,11,Fmonths later.
OL,13,FThe BBC ` and the country ` were in a
OL,14,Fvery difficult situation in 1975 when
OL,15,Fthe cut was made.
OL,17,FBut it's telling that the BBC did not
OL,18,Freverse this decision ` it was simply
OL,19,Fsuperseded by events years later.
OL,23,APub: 22-Jul-2025Qpppppppppppppppppppppp
OL,24,ANext Page BRewind CNat Radio FNat Sport
FL,125,120,200,300,0,100
PN,12408
SC,0008
CT,3,C
PS,c008
OL,0,        ECIMSBWebfax 2   F124A1772999460
OL,1,W{$~sj5j5h7}j7}                 G8/9
OL,2,W/*%+,"-/.!/*%/*-'Q(,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,
OL,3,GFEATURESCSuspension of daytime BBC Two
OL,4,Ctransmitter shutdown due to Channel 4
OL,5,Claunch
OL,6,
OL,7,FEven the experiment in late afternoon
OL,8,FTV from November 1981 to April 1982
OL,9,Fdidn't extend the time transmitters
OL,10,Fwere on air for. They merely curtailed
OL,11,Fthe afternoon trade test.
OL,13,FThe first evidence of a permanent
OL,14,Fextension to BBC Two airtime came in
OL,15,FDecember 1983. Ceefax was shown from
OL,16,F9am onwards when there were no schools
OL,17,Fprogrammes. This started to be
OL,18,Facknowledged in Radio Times a few weeks
OL,19,Flater.
OL,23,APub: 22-Jul-2025Qpppppppppppppppppppppp
OL,24,ANext Page BRewind CNat Radio FNat Sport
FL,125,120,200,300,0,100
PN,12409
SC,0009
CT,3,C
PS,c008
OL,0,        ECIMSBWebfax 2   F124A1772999460
OL,1,W{$~sj5j5h7}j7}                 G9/9
OL,2,W/*%+,"-/.!/*%/*-'Q(,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,
OL,3,GFEATURESCSuspension of daytime BBC Two
OL,4,Ctransmitter shutdown due to Channel 4
OL,5,Claunch
OL,6,
OL,7,FWas this to help the trade? Was this
OL,8,Fbecause a shutdown during school
OL,9,Fholidays alone was pointless? Was it
OL,10,Fpart of the drive to promote Ceefax
OL,11,Fduring otherwise empty airtime? Or was
OL,12,Fit to allow viewers with teletext sets
OL,13,Fto access the full BBC Two Ceefax
OL,14,Fmagazine all day?
OL,23,APub: 22-Jul-2025Qpppppppppppppppppppppp
OL,24,ANext Page BRewind CNat Radio FNat Sport
FL,125,120,200,300,0,100@
